open_project : Opens a project and shows its window. Takes a .framejob package, or any movie, sound file or picture — opening one of those builds a fresh UNTITLED project sized and rated to it with the file as the first clip on track 1, exactly as double-clicking it does. Answers already_open: true when that file is already open.

new_project : Creates a blank 1920×1080 / 30 fps project and shows its window — File ▸ New Project. With path it is saved there straight away (a .framejob extension is added if missing) so later calls can name it; without one it stays an untitled draft until save_project. Change the size and rate afterwards with set_canvas. A path another open project holds is refused, and nothing is created; close_project closes that one first.

detect_silence : Finds the quiet stretches of the timeline and REPORTS them, changing nothing — the read half of Clip ▸ Remove Silences…, whose Remove button sends the answer to ripple_delete_ranges. In voice mode (the default) a moment is quiet when the cached Silero VAD probability over it is under voice_confidence; a clip whose source window holds no voice anywhere, and every file when the model cannot be used, is judged by level — each 10 ms of the cached waveform times the audio envelope against threshold_db. In either mode a moment whose envelope alone puts full scale at or under threshold_db is quiet, so volume, fades, ducking, mute and another track's solo all count. A run quieter than threshold_db and at least min_length long is a candidate; it then loses padding at each end, and its bounds snap INWARD to the frame grid — which can leave a frame of room tone, where outward would clip the attack 

insert_graphic : Places a graphic clip at the playhead, as Insert ▸ Graphic…'s Insert does: on the front track when it fits there, else on a new track above everything, at the module's meta duration and size, as ONE undo step (Insert Graphic). A template (from template) is first copied into graphics/ under a free name (lower-third, lower-third-2, …), which is not undoable; a project module (from project) is placed as it is, with no copy. name in the reply is the module the clip is drawn by. A module that does not compile places nothing and is refused with its first error; the template's copy stays in graphics/. With a nest open the clip lands inside it. list_graphics lists what there is.

get_media_analysis : Answers an analysis of one media file, or of the part of it one clip plays, made ON THIS MAC — no network request, no upload, no API key — and kept per media in the project's cache, so a later call over a window already analysed answers at once. kind "shots" finds the hard cuts: cuts is [{frame, source}] sorted by time, frame the media's frame index and source its presentation time in the media's own SOURCE ticks (600000 per second, of the file played forwards), with count. A cut inside a gradual dissolve is not reported, and a single flash frame is not a cut; a dissolve between flat-coloured pictures (slides, title cards) can show as one cut. kind "masks" finds a person's outline in every frame (Vision's person segmentation, on the Mac) and answers its runs, never pixels: mask_size [w, h] (the masks' own size), frames (frames held in the window), subject_found (whether any frame holds a

get_timeline_transcript : Answers every word HEARD on the timeline (or inside the nest set_scope has open), in timeline order, nested clips included: words is [{text, start, end, clip, track, media, engine, filler, speaker?, editable, why?, id, cut_start, cut_end}], times in TIMELINE ticks (600000 per second), ordered by start, then end, then the front track first. A clip that is muted, soloed out or at volume 0 is not heard and gives no words. track is the timeline track the word plays on (a nested word's is its nest clip's). editable is false, with why, for a word inside a nest, under a transition or on a locked track. id {nest_path, media, source, k} names the word across edits: the nest clips it plays through, its media, its start in the media's SOURCE ticks as the recogniser put it and k, counting earlier words with the same three (0 unless one piece of the source plays twice). An engine apple word's start i

get_cursor_events : Answers what a screen recording's cursor file holds — its clicks, scrolls, shortcuts, typing stretches and, asked for, its path — read ON THIS MAC from the media's .fjcursor (get_project's media[].cursor). With media, times are the file's own SOURCE ticks (time "media"); with clip, they are ticks from the clip's start (time "clip", through its speed and ramp), and each click and scroll also has q [qx, qy]: its position in the clip's region frame — an offset in source pixels from the centre of the clip's cropped picture, the frame add_zoom_action's region takes, so a region around a click is {x: qx, y: qy, w, h}. x and y are the movie's own pixels from its top-left; size is [w, h]. clicks [{t, button (0 left, 1 right, 2 other), down (1 press, 0 release), count, x, y, q?}], scrolls [{t, x, y, dx, dy (points), q?}] (each a single wheel event), shortcuts [{t, keys, code}], typing [{from, to,

cancel_export : Stops an export this launch started — the Export Queue row's Cancel. A queued one is cancelled before it starts; a running one stops and its half-written file is removed, though the answer may still read running until the writer has stopped (export_status then reads cancelled). A finished one is left alone. Answers as export_status does.

